  journal  = "arXiv [cond-mat.mtrl-sci]",
  abstract = "The theoretical picture of thermal field-emission (TFE) from
              semiconductors has been limited to 1D and 2D models. This can be
              attributed to the complex and interdependent phenomena that is
              involved in TFE from semiconductors which makes the calculations
              cumbersome. Such limitations result in a partial understanding of
              the underlying physics of semiconducting surfaces under high
              electrical fields, which requires the addition of the temporal
              dimension (4D) to yield a realistic model. Here we develop a 3D
